  <h2 class="project-section-title">Challenges</h2>
  <h3 class="project-subsection-title">1. Singularity</h3>
  <p>
    In contact localization problems, singularity occurs when multiple pairs of contact points and force vectors result in the same sensor
    measurements. In particle filter (PF)-based algorithms, the resampling process leads the particles to converge to a single point, so they output
    only one solution even if there are multiple solutions which have low QP errors. The singularity is an inherent characteristic of the contact
    localization problem and cannot be entirely eliminated. Therefore, our goal is not to eliminate singularity, but to predict it more accurately:
    from a probabilistic perspective, the singularity suggests that the distribution of contact points is multi-modal.
  </p>
