  <h3 class="project-subsection-title">2. Finite observation time length</h3>
  <p>
    The multi-contact point localization problem can be formulated as estimating the posterior $p(\mathbf{r}_t \mid \mathbf{O}_{1:t}, \mathcal{S})$,
    conditioned on all past observations ($\mathbf{O}_{1:t}$) and the robot surfaces $\mathcal{S}$. However, this posterior cannot be directly
    addressed by a diffusion model, because the observation time length cannot be infinite. If two contacts occur sequentially, observations outside
    the time window contain important information about the first contact.
  </p>
